<article class="env-lemma" id="095X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/095X">Lemma <span data-tag="095X">59.76.2</span>.</a> Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. If $j : U \to X$ is an étale morphism of schemes, then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$K|_ U \in D_ c(U_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ if $K \in D_ c(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$j_!M \in D_ c(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ if $M \in D_ c(U_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ and the morphism $j$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first assertion is clear. The second follows from the fact that $j_!$ is exact and Lemma <a href="/tag/03S8" data-tag="03S8">59.73.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>